LANGUAGE English

Book Driveway Ordered No Keep
	
	Page Place 
		Triggered By @PlaceDriveway When Not testMod
		
		Add TileDriveway

		Text """
			It's 3:00 and you're on time. The man your friend spoke with on the
			phone--Benjamin--should be here to meet you.

			As you walk up the driveway, you can see how poorly maintained the
			house and grounds are. The drive is paved, but cracked and pocked.
			Weeds grow as high as your waist on either side and you briefly
			wonder what might be hiding there.

			Place the {c:TileDriveway} tile as indicated.
		"""
		
	End Page Place
	
	Page PlaceInvestigators
		Add TokenDrivewayInvestigators
		
		Text """
			You wonder what you were thinking when you said <<yes>> to your
			friend. Place your investigators as indicated.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenDrivewayInvestigators
	End Page PlaceInvestigators
	
	Page PlaceExploreKitchenViaDriveway
		Add TokenExploreKitchenViaDriveway!

		Text """
			After walking around the house, you are not surprised that the door
			next to you is covered with mud and spiderwebs. Like the rest of the
			house, the paint is peeling and the door shows signs of dry rot.

			Place an Explore token as indicated.
		"""
	
	End Page PlaceExploreKitchenViaDriveway
	
	Page PlaceGate
		Add TokenExploreBackyardViaDriveway!
		
		Text """
			Up ahead, at the end of the drive, is a gate that leads around to
			the back of the house. Place an Explore token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlaceGate
	
	Page PlaceGardenTool
		Add TokenSearchDrivewayGardenTool!

		Text """
			The weeds behind the house are even taller than the ones in front.
			Over at the corner of the drive, something under the weeds catches
			your eye. Place a Search token as indicated.	
		"""
		
		initialized = true
	End Page PlaceGardenTool
	
	Page PlaceWendy
		Page IS Visible When #HeroWendyAdams
		
		Add QItemWendyGun

		Text """
			As she walks up the drive, Wendy Adams trips and falls. She twists
			her ankle and skins her knees. When she looks up, she sees
			something in the weeds. Wendy gains the {c:QItemWendyGun}.

			When she finally stands up, she doesn’t feel as agile as usual. In
			this scenario, Wendy can become Restrained.
		"""
	End Page PlaceWendy
	
	Page PlaceTest No Text
		Page IS Visible When testMode
		
		Add TokenTestPlaceDriveway, TokenTestTakeBooks, TokenTestStartRitual
		Add TokenTestRitualPreparations, TokenTestRitualFinished
		Add TokenTestPlaceTortureChamber, TokenTestPlaceLibraryViaStudy
		Add TokenTestPlaceLibraryAfterCultists, TokenTestPlaceChapelViaLibrary
		Add TokenTestPlaceKitchenViaDiningRoom, TokenTestPlaceStudyViaHall2
		Add TokenTestPlaceHall2ViaHall1, TokenTestPlaceStudyViaFoyer
		Add TokenTestPlaceDungeonCell, TokenTestPlaceCryptViaDungeonCave
		Add TokenTestPlaceDiningRoomViaBackdoor, TokenTestPlaceCryptViaChapel
		Add TokenTestPlaceCoatRoomViaGallery, TokenTestPlaceAltar
		Add TokenTestInitChosenInvestigator, TokenTestPlaceDriveway
		Add TokenTestBasementViaDiningRoomSight, TileStudy, TileHall2
		Add TileGallery, TileFoyer, TileDriveway, TileDiningRoom, TileCrypt,
		Add TileChapel, TileBasement, TileBackyard, TileAltar
		Add TokenTestPlaceHall1ViaDiningRoom, TokenTestPlaceFoyerViaGallery
		Add TokenTestPlaceGalleryViaFoyer, TokenExploreHall2ViaFoyer
		Add TokenTestPlaceFoyerViaHall2, TokenTestPlaceStudyViaFoyer
		Add TokenTestPlaceStudyViaHall2, TokenTestPlaceFoyerViaStudy
		Add TokenTestPlaceHall2ViaFoyer, TokenTestPlaceDungeonCaveViaBasement
		Add TokenTestPlaceDungeonCaveViaCrypt, TokenTestPlaceHall1ViaHall2
		Add TokenTestPlaceBackdoorViaDriveway, TokenTestPlaceGalleryViaHall1
		Add TokenTestJournal2, TokenTestBenTrigger, TileHall1
		Add TileTortureChamber, TokenBackyardBenBefore, TokenBackyardBenAfter
		Add TokenBackyardBenPassive, TokenTestBackdoorLocked
		
		Exit
	End Page PlaceTest
	
	
	Page SearchGardenTool
		Triggered By @SearchDrivewayGardenTool
		
		Prolog """
			The weeds along the edge of driveway are tall, thick, and
			long-dead. Whatever is under them has been bound tightly over
			the years.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Add QItemGardenTool
		Remove TokenSearchDrivewayGardenTool

		Text """
			You rustle around in the weeds and find something interesting.
			Gain the {c:QItemGardenTool} Common Item, then discard this
			Search token.

			As you pull it free of the weeds, a child's doll is exposed.
			The clothing is ragged and the paint is chipped. You think
			back to the children who were found here and wonder if this
			doll belonged to one of them.

			Gain 1 {clue}, then take 1 facedown Horror ({will} negates).
		"""
		
		foundGardenTool = true		
		Exit
	End Page SearchGardenTool
	
	Page SearchJournal
		Triggered By @SearchOutsideJournal
		
		Prolog "Benjamin dropped a book here."
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchDrivewayJournal

		Text """
			Up close you can see that it is thin and leather-bound. You
			pick it up and flip through the pages:  it's a journal. The
			first entry was scrawled last Sunday. You should give it back
			to Benjamin, but maybe you can take a quick look first.

			Gain the {c:QItemJournal} Unique Item, then discard this Search
			token. An investigator holding the {c:QItemJournal} can
			interact with it in the app.
		"""
		
		foundJournal = true
		Exit
	End Page SearchJournal	
	
	Page ExploreBackyardViaDriveway
		Triggered By @ExploreBackyardViaDriveway
		
		Text """
			An intricate wrought-iron gate is set into a stone wall.
			Like the rest of the house, the paint is peeling and the
			bars are rusting. The gate looks like it was
			exceptionally strong at one time, but maybe not now.

			It probably wouldn't take much effort to push it open 
			({strength}).
		"""
		
		Test Quota 3 Set exploredBackyardNotNicely
		If exploredBackyardNotNicely Then Goto ExploreNotNice
		Goto ExploreNice
	End Page ExploreBackyardViaDriveway
	
	Page ExploreNotNice
		Add TokenDriveWayBen!
		Remove TokenExploreBackyardViaDriveway

		Text """
			You give it all you've got... and the gate, seemingly
			rusty and poorly maintained, gives way with a terrible
			crash. As the noise echoes down the drive, an angry
			man storms around the corner and strides up behind you.

			Place the Purple Man token as indicated; this is
			Benjamin Smythe, the man your friend spoke with on the
			phone.
			
			Discard this Explore token.
		"""
		
		exploredBackyardNicely = false
	End Page ExploreNotNice
	
	Page ExploreNotNiceBen
		Text """
			As you turn to look at Benjamin, you hear a second crash
			behind the gate.

			<<What are you doing?! I just had that rehung yesterday!>>
			he yells. <<I hired you to help us get this house ready
			for sale, not destroy it. You were to meet me here; I'm
			not sure why you thought it was a good idea to start
			without me.>>

			Benjamin brushes past you with a harrumph. Discard the
			Purple Man token.

			You’ve only just arrived and the client is already angry.
			This could turn out badly for both you and your friend's
			business.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenDrivewayBen
	End Page ExploreNotNiceBen
	
	Page ExploreNotNiceJournal
		Add TokenSearchDrivewayJournal!, TokenExploreBackyardViaDrivewaySight!
		
		Text """
			You look down and shake your head. As you do, you see a book lying
			on the ground where Benjamin had been standing. Place a Search token
			as indicated.
			
			You turn back to the gate, take a breath and...
			
			Place a Sight token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page ExploreNotNiceJournal
	
	Page ExploreNice
		Remove TokenExploreBackyardViaDriveway
		Add TokenDrivewayBen!

		Text """
			As you gently pull the gate, you find that it opens easily.
			Now that you're looking, you see that someone recently
			cleaned the hinges and gave them some oil. You're glad you
			didn't force it. Remove this explore token.

			
			<<I see the handyman was able to fix the gate yesterday.
			That will make things easier.>> You start, not having
			heard the man walk up behind you.
			
			Place the Purple Man token as indicated.
		"""
		
		exploredBackyardNicely = true
	End Page ExploreNice
	
	Page ExploreNiceBen
		Text """
			You turn to meet the eyes of an aging but vigorous man. He
			introduces himself as Benjamin Smythe, the man whom your
			friend spoke with. <<You'll want to follow me so we can
			get started.>>
			
			Benjamin turns and walks through the now-open gate.
			
			Remove the Purple Man token from the board.
		"""
	
		Remove TokenDrivewayBen
	End Page ExploreNiceBen
	
	Page ExploreNiceJournal
		Add TokenSearchDrivewayJournal!, TokenExploreBackyardViaDrivewaySight!

		Text """
			You turn to look back and see a book Benjamin must have
			dropped. Place a Search token as indicated.

			A moment later, you hear Benjamin yelp, followed by a loud crash.
			You quickly turn back toward the gate. Place a Sight token as
			indicated.
		"""
	
		Exit
	End Page ExploreNiceJournal
End Book Driveway